          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Return Mail, Inc., return Mail, Inc. argues that the term \u201cperson\u201d does not include the United States government, relying on the Dictionary Act definition and the Court\u2019s presumptive definition of \u201cperson.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "25b98ea226342e1d279a03475bdffa42c832e9ff965ca654c11afa808411b936",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-25b98ea22634-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice GORSUCH, justice GORSUCH questioned why Congress would allow the government to initiate ex parte review before an agency but not permit a more adversarial process involving the government as a party."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "25b98ea226342e1d279a03475bdffa42c832e9ff965ca654c11afa808411b936",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-25b98ea22634-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked why the definition of \u201cperson\u201d in the ex parte reexamination context cannot simply exclude the government."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "25b98ea226342e1d279a03475bdffa42c832e9ff965ca654c11afa808411b936",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-25b98ea22634-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kavanaugh asked whether executive\u2011branch agencies can always communicate with one another."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "25b98ea226342e1d279a03475bdffa42c832e9ff965ca654c11afa808411b936",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-25b98ea22634-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 65,
              "start": 65
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, justice Kagan questioned the presumption that \u201cperson\u201d is a stable default rule and whether Congress would legislate against it."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "25b98ea226342e1d279a03475bdffa42c832e9ff965ca654c11afa808411b936",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-25b98ea22634-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 66,
